{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>לחת.</b> Written defective, to say that both were equal, and two corresponding to heaven and earth, and corresponding to groom and bride, and corresponding to two attendants — five commandments on one tablet and five on the other tablet, corresponding to the five fifths of the Torah, and both of them ten corresponding to the ten utterances with which the world was created. And in Eruvin in the chapter כיצד מעברין: Rabbi Elazar said, what is written ״לוחת אבן״ — if a person makes himself like stone, his learning endures in his hand, and if not, his learning does not endure in his hand. And Rabbi Elazar said, what is written ״חרות על הלוחת״ — had the first tablets not been broken, Torah would not have been forgotten from Israel. Rav Acha said, also no nation and tongue would rule over them, as it is said ״חרות״ — do not read חרות but חירות."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "The lemma לחת and quoted forms לוחת reflect the defective spelling without vav; the translations preserve the defective forms as they appear in the source."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:04:29.610334408Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}